Build Tiny Tcl 6.8.1 with Open Watcom C for 16-bit DOS (docs/M1-REPORT.md,
section 4). Upstream builds with Borland C 5.0.

- Include "tcldos.h" by its real name: upstream writes "tclDos.h", which a
  case-sensitive host filesystem does not find.
- Do not include Borland's <values.h>; tclExtdInt.h has fallbacks for the
  MAXINT family.
- Take errno, sys_nerr and environ from the C library's headers rather than
  redeclaring them with different modifiers; drop tclEnv.c's
  "#define environ _environ".
- Rename tclEnv.c's private setenv/unsetenv, which manipulate environ for
  the env array, to static TclSetEnv/TclUnsetEnv, so that they do not
  collide with the C library's; the one three-argument call loses its
  stray third argument.
- TclX_InitGeneral is void: do not return TCL_OK from it.
- DOS has no symbolic links: undefine S_IFLNK and S_ISLNK, which Open
  Watcom's <sys/stat.h> defines, so that lstat is stat and there is no
  "file readlink".
- Include <io.h> and <direct.h> for read() and getcwd(): unprototyped,
  getcwd() is taken to return int, which loses the segment of a far
  pointer.

